---
import '@labcat/crt/glow.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>@labcat/crt playground</title>
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A subtle CRT phosphor effect for the web. Editorial restraint, three tunable presets."
    />
    <style is:global>
      :root {
        color-scheme: dark;
        background: #0d0d0d;
        color: #d5d5d5;
        --pg-bezel: #050505;
      }
      html,
      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
      }
      body {
        font-family:
          'Berkeley Mono', ui-monospace, 'JetBrains Mono', SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas,
          monospace;
      }
      crt-overlay {
        padding: var(--pg-overlay-padding, 4rem 6vw);
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      /* Only the article matching the overlay's preset renders. Default
         (no attribute) maps to calm. */
      crt-overlay > article[data-preset] {
        display: none;
      }
      crt-overlay[preset='calm'] > article[data-preset='calm'],
      crt-overlay:not([preset]) > article[data-preset='calm'],
      crt-overlay[preset='warm'] > article[data-preset='warm'],
      crt-overlay[preset='cool'] > article[data-preset='cool'] {
        display: block;
      }

      h1.crt-glow {
        font-family: 'Berkeley Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace;
        font-size: 2.25rem;
        margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
        color: var(--crt-glow-color, #f0f0f0);
        letter-spacing: 0.005em;
        line-height: 1.15;
        font-weight: 500;
      }
      p,
      pre,
      blockquote {
        line-height: 1.7;
        max-width: 64ch;
        margin: 0.85rem 0;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
      }
      code.crt-glow {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 0 0.25em;
        background: var(--pg-code-bg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05));
        color: var(--crt-glow-color, #f0f0f0);
      }
      pre.code {
        white-space: pre;
        background: var(--pg-code-bg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04));
        padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
        color: var(--crt-glow-color, #f0f0f0);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.55;
        overflow-x: auto;
        max-width: 72ch;
        border-left: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 25%, transparent);
      }
      blockquote {
        border-left: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 25%, transparent);
        padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1.25rem;
        margin-left: 0;
        font-style: italic;
        max-width: 60ch;
      }
      .citation {
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
        opacity: 0.55;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        margin: 0 0 2rem;
      }

      .drop-zone {
        margin: 2.5rem 0 0.5rem;
        max-width: 600px;
        min-height: 140px;
        border: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 25%, transparent);
        border-radius: 2px;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        text-align: center;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        box-sizing: border-box;
        position: relative;
        transition: border-color 160ms ease, background 160ms ease;
      }
      .drop-zone:empty::before {
        content: '⊕  add a photo  ·  tap or drop';
        opacity: 0.5;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      }
      .drop-zone img {
        display: block;
        max-width: 100%;
        max-height: 360px;
        object-fit: contain;
      }
      .drop-zone[data-dragover='true'] {
        border-color: currentColor;
        background: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 6%, transparent);
      }
      .drop-zone .remove-btn {
        position: absolute;
        top: 0.5rem;
        right: 0.5rem;
        appearance: none;
        background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
        color: inherit;
        border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 40%, transparent);
        font: inherit;
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
        cursor: pointer;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <playground-app>
      <crt-overlay preset="calm">
        <!-- calm: Thoreau, Walden, 1854. Project Gutenberg eBook #205, public domain. -->
        <article data-preset="calm">
          <p class="citation">Henry David Thoreau · Walden · 1854</p>
          <h1 class="crt-glow">Where I Lived, and What I Lived For</h1>
          <p>
            I went to the woods because I wished to live deliberately, to front only the essential
            facts of life, and see if I could not learn what it had to teach, and not, when I came
            to die, discover that I had not lived.
          </p>
          <p>
            I did not wish to live what was not life, living is so dear; nor did I wish to
            practise resignation, unless it was quite necessary. I wanted to live deep and suck
            out all the marrow of life, to live so sturdily and Spartan-like as to put to rout
            all that was not life, to cut a broad swath and shave close, to drive life into a
            corner, and reduce it to its lowest terms.
          </p>
          <div class="drop-zone"></div>
        </article>

        <!-- warm: Rumi, Masnavi I:1-4 (Reed-Flute). Nicholson translation 1925, public domain. -->
        <article data-preset="warm">
          <p class="citation">Jalal ad-Din Rumi · Masnavi I · trans. R. A. Nicholson · 1925</p>
          <h1 class="crt-glow">The Song of the Reed</h1>
          <blockquote>
            <p>
              Listen to the reed how it tells a tale, complaining of separations—
            </p>
            <p>
              Saying, "Ever since I was parted from the reed-bed, my lament hath caused man and
              woman to moan.
            </p>
            <p>
              I want a bosom torn by severance, that I may unfold the pain of love-desire.
            </p>
            <p>
              Every one who is left far from his source wishes back the time when he was united
              with it."
            </p>
          </blockquote>
          <div class="drop-zone"></div>
        </article>

        <!-- cool: Snow Crash epigraph (Neal Stephenson, 1992, short fair-use
             excerpt) framing bytes.Equal from the Go standard library
             (BSD-3-Clause, © The Go Authors). -->
        <article data-preset="cool">
          <p class="citation">Neal Stephenson · Snow Crash · 1992  //  The Go Authors · BSD-3-Clause</p>
          <blockquote>
            <p>
              When you are wrestling for possession of a sword, the man with the handle
              always wins.
            </p>
          </blockquote>
          <h1 class="crt-glow">bytes.Equal</h1>
          <p>
            Reports whether a and b have the same length and contain the same bytes. A nil
            argument is equivalent to an empty slice.
          </p>
          <pre class="code"><span class="crt-glow">func Equal(a, b []byte) bool &lbrace;
    return string(a) == string(b)
&rbrace;</span></pre>
          <div class="drop-zone"></div>
        </article>
      </crt-overlay>
    </playground-app>

    <script>
      import '@labcat/crt';
      import '../components/playground-app.ts';
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
